WEBVTT

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.820
<i>The Digimon Encyclopedia!</i>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.330
<i>Tentomon.</i>

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.450
<i>This Digimon is my partner.</i>

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.410
LEVEL:ROOKIE

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.330
<i>There are thin wings underneath the shell,</i>

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.290
TYPE: INSECT

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.250
<i>and Tentomon flies me wherever I want!</i>

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.250
SPECIAL MOVE: PETIT THUNDER

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.790
<i>Now, let's check this out!</i>

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.630
<i>Tentomon speaks in a Kansai dialect
for some reason,</i>

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.590
<i>and often says, "Dossei."
I wonder what it means...</i>

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.800
<i>I'll ask next time!</i>

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>Which Digimon will it be next time?</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.280
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.090
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:21.310
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:21.350
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.740
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:42.620
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:42.580
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:47.790
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.720
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.670
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.380
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:04.310
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:13.070
<i>Cannonbeemon was capturing Funbeemon
to turn them into their foot soldiers.</i>

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.200
<i>That was when Sora's group
happened to pass by.</i>

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.280
<i>However, Joe and Gomamon were captured.</i>

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:33.290
<i>To save Joe, Gomamon, and Funbeemon,</i>

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.130
<i>the children took on Cannonbeemon
and succeeded in their rescue!</i>

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.770
<i>And in that battle,</i>

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.310
<i>Birdramon super evolved into Garudamon.</i>

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.870
I could carry everyone anytime!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:08.010
It's okay, it'll be tough
if you fly all the time.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:09.880
You need to rest too.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.830
That's right.
Now, you get on too, Piyomon.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.000
Okay! All right then!

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.050
Why don't you guys come hop on too?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.220
It's nice and high, and comfy up here!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.510
Yamato, he's calling us.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.730
It's almost like a hammock!

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.110
Joe, you're gonna fall again.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.980
Hey! Yamato-kun!

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.360
You working out your legs?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.290
Oh, I get it!

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:41.870
You're taking on the scouting duty for us!

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.080
Yamato?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.170
It's fine.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:44.990
Hm?

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.910
What's "scouting"?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.240
I don't know.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.920
You don't?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.500
Okay, seeing as I'm the oldest,
I'll teach you. Pay attention...

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:02.510
<i>The cause of the major power outage
in the metropolitan area is still unclear.</i>

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.220
<i>Accidents and disasters
are occurring in many areas.</i>

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:12.230
<i>Fire officials have reported that they are
struggling to extinguish ongoing fires.</i>

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.940
<i>Please be extra cautious around flames.</i>

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.530
<i>"Your phone could not make this call."</i>

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.610
<i>The number of people trapped
inside elevators,</i>

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.030
<i>waiting to be rescued are also growing.</i>

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:27.790
<i>To those living in a housing complex
or are currently inside a building,</i>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.030
<i>"I'm trapped in an elevator."</i>

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:31.870
<i>please check your nearest elevators.</i>

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.030
LOW BATTERY

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.040
PLEASE CHARGE

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.550
THE KINGS OF THE INSECTS CLASH

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.810
This place looks crazy.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.350
It's like a natural maze.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.440
Yeah.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.810
There's a ton of squiggly paths
branching out everywhere.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.200
What if we get lost and can't get out?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.000
I'm scared!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.070
Don't worry. They say there's no puzzle
that can't be solved.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.450
So this maze will surely...

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.580
Oh... again.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.580
The reception...

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:20.210
Well, I'll guide you from above
if the time comes.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.430
Getting lost is one thing,
but let's try not to get separated either.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:25.760
With this geography,

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:29.390
we may not be able to communicate
with the Digivices.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.010
That's true...

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:35.190
Palmon, your face looks weird!

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.600
Mimi, your face looks weird too!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.190
My face doesn't look like this!

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.110
What's the matter, you two?

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.240
Look, look!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.360
It's funny!

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.450
Everybody's face looks weird!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.120
They have these at amusement parks often.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:57.380
It seems when the inner minerals
that make up the rocks are exposed,

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.040
they act like mirrors.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.130
Let me analyze it.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.170
Oh...

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.130
That's right...

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.510
Hm...

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.520
That's...

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.520
Taichi!

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.430
Something's coming!

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:23.900
Look!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.400
KUWAGAMON

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.360
That Digimon is...

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.410
No good. I can't look anything up!

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.910
Koshiro-san, that's Kuwagamon!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.000
They're a very nasty lot!

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.420
Over here too!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:51.430
One, two, three, four... five of them?!

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.600
We're trapped!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.560
Here they come!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.320
Palmon Evolution!

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.010
Tentomon Evolution!

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.070
Agumon Evolution!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.160
Togemon!

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.330
Kabuterimon!

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.700
Greymon!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.840
Prickly Bang-Bang!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.430
Togemon!

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:35.890
What was that?!

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.640
That was super sharp!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:45.980
Let's see who's stronger!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.400
Kabuterimon!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.590
Mega Blaster!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:18.850
Kabuterimon!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:25.400
Kabuterimon has a chance
if it's one-on-one!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.860
If I could just read their coordination!

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.870
Coconut Counter!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.010
Taichi-san!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.590
Mimi-chan, Togemon, thanks!

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.390
Kabuterimon?!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.890
I'm fine...

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:01.890
Koshiro!

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:06.730
Those Kuwagamon look like
they're attacking randomly,

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.270
but they're moving according
to each other's exact positions.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.900
This is just like...

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.400
a hunt!

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:19.700
Then does that mean we're their prey?
This is a real bugger...

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:34.760
If it's this narrow,
they can't swarm over us like flies now!

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.180
Until we completely shake them off,
we can't relax...

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.320
I just hope it isn't a dead-end
up ahead...

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.680
What?!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.110
Koshiro, they're gonna catch up to us.
Let's keep going.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.070
Yes...

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.540
OUKUWAMON

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.790
Jeez, what is it now?!

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:16.010
That's an Ultimate Digimon, Oukuwamon!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:20.010
This guy's no joke!

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.310
We were cornered to this spot!

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.730
Is everyone okay?!

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:36.500
Yes!

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.570
But everything hurts!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:43.950
Togemon!

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.930
Greymon! Kabuterimon!

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:04.970
Ugh, I'm at my limit!
Can't we do something?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.770
We got no chance if we're surrounded.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.440
Let's penetrate the enemy lines
and break free!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.480
You mean let's run for now?
Okay, I'm all for it!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.400
If I could just... use this!

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.490
Now! Run!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.640
Taichi-san, Mimi-san, do you hear me?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.100
It's no use...

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.530
Koshiro-san, make sure to hold on!

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.410
Greymon, you okay?!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:08.540
Yeah...

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:18.210
We can't do anything at this rate!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:21.480
Togemon!

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:23.300
Mega Flame!

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.430
Mimi-chan, you all right?!

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:32.310
Jeez! This maze and Kuwagamon,
I hate them all!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.820
Looks like they heard you.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:41.570
I'm sorry! But I do hate them!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.910
We've shaken them off somehow...

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.250
We need to hurry and rejoin everyone.

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:52.790
If we fly high, we'll get caught by them.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.330
We'll have to move through this maze.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:56.970
Yeah.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:00.840
Koshiro-san,
can I ask you to guide me through it?

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:04.470
Koshiro-san?

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.600
I can't...

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.600
If this doesn't work, I can't analyze it.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.180
I can't even collect data...

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.790
What a persistent fellow!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.330
If that's the case, I'll take you on!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.460
Kabuterimon!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.630
This is digital spirit!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:48.720
Not yet!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.760
Mega Blaster!

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.710
Koshiro-san...

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.270
Kabuterimon!

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:48.240
There's nothing left I can do...

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.950
Koshiro-san...

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.080
You... still have...

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.080
something left...

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.010
The most ultimate weapon...

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.880
that won't even lose to a tablet!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:09.800
That's...

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.420
your brain, Koshiro-san!

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.100
Your knowledge!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:15.560
That's right.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.230
It's your own self, Koshiro-san!

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:33.120
Kabuterimon,
shoot that crack on the upper right!

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.580
All right!

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.180
Here.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.470
Thank you.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:04.860
I was so desperate
to be everyone's help all the time...

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:10.860
It became default for me
to always make judgements through this.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:16.120
I had forgotten about my own self

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.910
who was sitting in front of the monitor.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.870
Until you reminded me, Kabuterimon.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:29.510
Even machines have days
when they don't feel well, like humans.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:35.180
When that happens, you just have to
reassess your abilities and overcome!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.520
Greymon and everyone's agility...

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.440
Kuwagamon's attack pattern...

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.440
Kabuterimon!

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:48.570
Search the area not far
from where we got separated,

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.860
focusing on narrow paths and dead ends!

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:54.200
Good, good! Koshiro-san!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:59.080
Work your brain at full speed!
I'm feelin' it!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.170
Kabuterimon...

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:12.630
Super Evolution!

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.400
Togemon!

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.240
That's...

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.120
Wow!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.950
Atlurkabuterimon...

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:47.500
At your service!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.330
ATLURKABUTERIMON

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:50.380
Is everyone all right?!

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.920
Koshiro! Kabuterimon became
an Ultimate Digimon too!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.020
Oukuwamon!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:09.860
All right, now let's finish this up
in an open space!

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:10.810
Yeah!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.450
You're not getting away!

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:17.820
Togemon!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.500
Taichi-san! Mimi-san!

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.830
Please use those mirror rocks!

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.490
Confuse them with our reflections
on the mirrors!

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.840
It should break their coordination!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.140
If you go left, right,
then left from there,

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:41.360
you should get to that place full
of the mirror rocks you found!

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:42.390
Got it!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:43.430
Togemon!

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.600
Hey, c'mon!

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.820
Oh, no!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.790
Just kidding!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.830
Togemon!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.460
Prickly Bang-Bang!

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.340
The Kuwagamon are confused!

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.590
It's just as Koshiro said!

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.140
Greymon...

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:35.270
Super Evolution!

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.710
Metalgreymon!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.550
Giga Storm!

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:07.540
So, Koshiro-san,
what's the plan on our side?

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:08.850
Of course!

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:14.360
It's a head-on battle with all the power
you have, Atlurkabuterimon!

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:15.860
All right!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.490
Good!

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:18.360
Good!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.510
Good! Good!

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.610
Good!

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:29.290
Let's have you taste
my fresh new super evolution!

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:34.790
Horn...

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:42.680
Buster!

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.730
Yes!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.410
Yeah!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.710
I knew Koshiro was awesome!

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.330
A friend in need is a friend indeed!

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.090
Yes!

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:20.470
Uh-huh! Good, good!

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:21.460
Oh!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.170
Huh?

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:24.640
It's fixed!

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:25.800
Really?!

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.470
Good thing!

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:29.300
Huh?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:30.890
What's wrong?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.480
It's... kind of faster now!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:36.480
Mm-hmm! Very, very good!

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.940
That's my servant!

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.110
He fell asleep...

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.950
He must've gotten tired from talking
to Yamato the whole time.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.700
Let's just let him sleep.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:49.790
Yeah.

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:51.500
It's gotten quiet, huh?

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:52.410
Hm?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.580
Let's get on now.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.750
What? Uh... yeah.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:15.730
<i>naze ima kono te to te nigitte</i>

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:15.770
<i>Why do these held hands</i>

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:18.440
<i>And the warmth exchanged</i>

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:18.400
<i>tashikameta taion wo</i>

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:20.860
<i>Make me reminisce now</i>

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:20.860
<i>natsukashiku omou noka</i>

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:26.450
<i>naze samidare no susabu shinen</i>

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:26.490
<i>Why an abyss dancing with endless rain</i>

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:29.030
<i>The gaze of that smile</i>

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:29.030
<i>hohoenda sono shisen ni</i>

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:30.320
<i>nakitaku naru</i>

00:22:29.030 --> 00:22:30.370
<i>Makes me want to cry</i>

00:22:30.370 --> 00:22:33.240
<i>So call me with that voice</i>

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:33.240
<i>sono koe de boku wo yonde kure</i>

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:35.460
<i>This weakness I cannot tell others</i>

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:35.410
<i>dare ni ienu kono yowasa ga</i>

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:38.540
<i>I realize is my pillar to stand firm</i>

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:38.500
<i>tsuyoku tatsu tame no jiku dato omoishiru</i>

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:40.840
<i>Difference is what makes me adore you</i>

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:40.790
<i>chigau kara itooshiku naru</i>

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:43.800
<i>I just want to understand you and me</i>

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:43.750
<i>tada wakaritai kimi to boku wo</i>

00:22:43.800 --> 00:22:46.010
<i>Scars grow the more we live</i>

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:45.960
<i>ikiru hodo kizu ga fuete iku</i>

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:49.260
<i>But still we seek the reasons for us</i>

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:49.220
<i>sore demo sagashiteiru bokura no wake wo</i>

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:51.520
<i>Overlaying them makes us beautiful</i>

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:51.470
<i>kasanete wa utsukushiku naru</i>

00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:55.390
<i>I want to know now, I want to cry out</i>

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:55.390
<i>ima wakaritai sakebi dashitai</i>

00:23:01.730 --> 00:23:04.610
<i>Garurumon dashes. Joe slides.</i>

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:08.360
<i>Joe and Ikkakumon stand up
against Yamato and Sora's danger!</i>

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:12.450
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"Zudomon's Iron Hammer of Lightning"</i>

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:15.240
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
